# Minecraft Fabric Mod Development Rules

## Project Context
You are working on a Minecraft Fabric mod project with the following structure:
- Fabric mod for Minecraft 1.21
- Uses Fabric Loader 0.16.9+ and Fabric API
- Java 21 required
- Gradle build system with Fabric Loom
- CI/CD via GitHub Actions (if configured)
- Basic Storage mod for vanilla-friendly mass item storage

## Key Technologies
- **Language**: Java 21
- **Build Tool**: Gradle with Fabric Loom
- **Framework**: Fabric (Minecraft modding)
- **Testing**: Minecraft test server via build.ps1
- **Dependencies**: Fabric API (required)
- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions (if configured)
- **Publishing**: Modrinth, GitHub Releases (if configured)

## Project Structure
```
mod-basic-storage/
├── src/main/java/          # Java source code
│   └── com/khazoda/basicstorage/
│       ├── BasicStorage.java           # Main mod class
│       ├── BasicStorageClient.java     # Client class
│       ├── block/                      # Block implementations
│       ├── item/                       # Item implementations
│       ├── registry/                   # Registry classes
│       ├── storage/                    # Storage system
│       ├── util/                       # Utilities
│       └── datagen/                    # Data generation
├── src/main/resources/     # Resources (mixins, fabric.mod.json)
├── scripts/                # Utility scripts
├── gradle.properties       # Mod configuration
└── build.gradle           # Build configuration
```

## Namespace Convention
- **Organization**: com.khazoda
- **Mod ID**: basicstorage
- **JAR Name**: basicstorage
- **Java Package**: com.khazoda.basicstorage
- **Maven Group**: com.khazoda

## Configuration Management
All mod properties are centralized in `gradle.properties`:
- Minecraft/Fabric versions
- Mod metadata (name, version, ID, etc.)
- Dependencies
- Use property expansion in fabric.mod.json and build.gradle

## Development Workflow
1. Make changes to Java code or resources
2. Run `.\build.ps1` to build
3. Run `.\build.ps1 -StartServer` to test with local server (if available)
4. Commit changes (mod will be built by CI if configured)
5. Tag releases for automatic publishing

## Build Scripts
- **build.ps1**: Main build script
  - Sets up Java 21 environment
  - Builds mod
  - Optionally starts test server with mod
  - Downloads MC server & Fabric loader automatically

## Code Style
- Follow Java conventions
- Use meaningful variable names
- Minimize comments (self-documenting code)
- Use existing patterns in codebase
- NEVER add comments unless explicitly requested

## Language-Specific Rules
**IMPORTANT**: User rules mention TypeScript standards, but this is a **Java project**. The following clarifications apply:

### TypeScript Rules (Not Applicable)
- User rules about TypeScript types (`any`, `!`, `as unknown as T`) do NOT apply to Java code
- Java has its own type system and conventions
- Follow Java type conventions and patterns

### String Formatting Rules
- User rules specify double quotes and string templates for TypeScript/JavaScript
- **For Java code**: Use standard Java string conventions:
  - Double quotes (`"`) for string literals (standard Java)
  - String concatenation with `+` is acceptable and common in Java
  - String formatting with `String.format()` or `MessageFormat` for complex formatting
  - StringBuilder for performance-critical string building
  - String templates (Java 21+) can be used but are optional
- **For TypeScript/JavaScript files** (if any): Follow user rules (double quotes, templates)

## Testing
- Use local test server via build.ps1
- Test both client and server functionality
- Verify crate creation and item storage
- Test crate station GUI functionality

## Common Tasks
- **Add new block**: Update BlockRegistry.java and register block
- **Add new item**: Update ItemRegistry.java and register item
- **Modify storage behavior**: Update CrateStorage.java
- **Change GUI**: Update CrateStationBlockEntity.java
- **Release new version**: Update mod_version in gradle.properties, commit, tag, push

## Important Files
- `gradle.properties`: Central configuration
- `src/main/resources/fabric.mod.json`: Mod metadata
- `src/main/java/com/khazoda/basicstorage/BasicStorage.java`: Main mod class
- `src/main/java/com/khazoda/basicstorage/storage/CrateStorage.java`: Storage logic
- `src/main/java/com/khazoda/basicstorage/block/entity/CrateStationBlockEntity.java`: GUI logic
